      "output": "The **approximate monthly EMI** for a ₹5,00,000 loan at **10% annual interest** for **3 years** is calculated as follows:\n\n---\n\n### **Step-by-Step Calculation**\nThe standard **reducing-balance EMI formula** is:\n\n\\[\nEMI = P \\times \\frac{r \\times (1 + r)^n}{(1 + r)^n - 1}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( P = ₹5,00,000 \\) (loan principal)\n- \\( r = \\frac{10\\%}{12} = 0.8333\\% \\) (monthly interest rate)\n- \\( n = 3 \\times 12 = 36 \\) (total number of monthly installments)\n\n#### **1. Monthly Interest Rate (\\( r \\))**\n\\[\nr = \\frac{10\\%}{12} = 0.008333\n\\]\n\n#### **2. EMI Calculation**\n\\[\nEMI = 500000 \\times \\frac{0.008333 \\times (1 + 0.008333)^{36}}{(1 + 0.008333)^{36} - 1}\n\\]\n\nUsing the calculator, the EMI is approximately:\n**₹16,133.59 per month**.\n\n---\n\n### **Total Repayment Over 3 Years**\n\\[\n\\text{Total Repayment} = EMI \\times n = 16133.59 \\times 36 = ₹5,80,809.24\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### **Summary**\n- **Monthly EMI:** **₹16,134 (approximate)**\n- **Total Amount Paid Over 3 Years:** **₹5,80,809 (approximate)**"
